  "result": "The gate returned **OK** on the third of its six allowed runs: 7 witnesses, 9 names, no composed rules.\n\n**What the rule says**\n- **Applies when:** the subject, a vehicle in the \"traffic\" group, occupies a centre turn lane c.\n- **Obligation:** at every centre turn lane the subject occupies, its presence must be explained one of two ways:\n  - **\"From the highway\":** at that moment, the subject declares it will turn left at an intersection or driveway/alley entrance on the same highway as c.\n  - **\"Onto the highway\":** the subject has stayed in c ever since a completed left turn was recognised there (`drv.motion.left_turn`, using the four turn parameters). At some moment in the 10 s turn window before that turn, it was off the highway that c lies on.\n\n**Gate runs**\n1. **UNANCHORED_VARIABLE:** the intersection and driveway regions were linked to the subject only through the declared intention, and that doesn't count as a link. I fixed it by requiring those regions to lie on the same highway as c, using `st.on_way`, which the node already claims.\n2. **WITNESS_FAIL:** in the turning scenes, the vehicle's heading didn't match the turn its yaw rate implied. I set the headings to match and shortened those traces so the vehicle stays inside the lane after the turn.\n3. **OK.**\n\n**Choices the node left open**\n- **Same-highway link (please check):** the blueprint says only \"some intersection or driveway/alley entrance\". I read \"the highway\" in \"onto or from the highway\" as the highway the centre turn lane is on. The consequence is that a declared left turn at an intersection on a different highway no longer excuses being in the lane. I didn't declare this as a narrowing, so the planner should confirm this reading.\n- **\"Traffic\" group:** the node gives it no road user of its own, so I attached it to the subject. Every vehicle class is in that group, so this excludes nothing.\n\n**Witnesses**\n- **The five the node planned:** `forbid`, `permit`, `idle`, `blind` and `branch_1`.\n- **Two I added to cover branches the planned five don't reach:**\n  - `branch_2` (compliant): the declared left turn is at an intersection rather than a driveway.\n  - `branch_3` (violated): the same 85° left turn into the lane, but starting from the highway's own shoulder, so the \"was off the highway\" check fails.\n\nFiles are in `library/` (paths relative to the repository root):\n- `library/TrafficSpec/Rules/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_223_3a.lean`\n- `library/TrafficSpecWitness/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_223_3a.lean`\n- `task_result.md`, in the working directory",
